<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morioka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morioka is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwate-prefecture">Iwate Prefecture</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. It grew up as the castle town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanbu-clan">Nanbu clan</a>, who moved their seat there at the end of the 16th century and built Morioka Castle in stages over several decades, and it was the centre of the Morioka domain throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>. It lies where the Nakatsu and Shizukuishi rivers join the Kitakami.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morioka.jpg" alt="Morioka" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 水だらけのプール · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morioka_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
